From ad0c07d98927eab0c5554236844ba041d8c8284d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Figueiredo <alex.fernandesfigueiredo@windriver.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:12:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 75/75] Add TLS ingress secret support to watcher

The watcher chart has no TLS support for its public endpoint: values.yaml
declares no secrets.tls tree, the manifests block has no
secret_ingress_tls toggle and the chart ships no secret-ingress-tls
template. helm-toolkit.manifests.ingress looks up
secrets.tls.<backendServiceType>.<backendService>.<endpoint> to name the
ingress TLS secret, so any TLS material set under
endpoints.infra_optim.host_fqdn_override.public.tls is ignored and the
public API stays HTTP-only without any error.

Add the same three pieces that other OpenStack-Helm charts carry:
  - secrets.tls.infra_optim.api.public naming the TLS secret
  - manifests.secret_ingress_tls toggle
  - templates/secret-ingress-tls.yaml delegating to
    helm-toolkit.manifests.secret_ingress_tls

The certificate material is supplied at run time through
endpoints.infra_optim.host_fqdn_override.public.tls (ca, crt, key). The
secret is only rendered when both crt and key are set, so the default
rendering is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Alex Figueiredo <alex.fernandesfigueiredo@windriver.com>
---
 watcher/templates/secret-ingress-tls.yaml | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 watcher/values.yaml                       |  5 +++++
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 watcher/templates/secret-ingress-tls.yaml

diff --git a/watcher/templates/secret-ingress-tls.yaml b/watcher/templates/secret-ingress-tls.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..212bbf2b5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/watcher/templates/secret-ingress-tls.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+{{/*
